[
  "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The scene features two matte white ceramic bowls placed on an aged, weathered oak tabletop, centered to allow for circular cropping. The camera angle is a 3/4 overhead view, capturing the full depth of the bowls. One bowl is in sharp focus in the foreground, while the second is softly blurred in the background. The dish consists of whole-wheat rotini pasta tossed in a creamy, pale white sauce made of ricotta and Greek yogurt, with bright green peas dispersed throughout. The sauce has a glossy, silken texture, clinging to the ridges of the pasta. Fresh, vibrant green basil leaves are folded through, adding pops of color, with subtle flecks of black pepper and bright yellow lemon zest visible on the surface. A few peas have tumbled slightly onto the wooden surface near a discarded, squeezed half-lemon and a small garlic clove. Soft, natural side light from a window to the left highlights the creaminess of the sauce and the texture of the pasta. The setting is a cozy, warm kitchen environment. Includes minor culinary imperfections: a small drop of sauce on the rim of the foreground bowl, a few stray crumbs of pasta, and non-symmetrical, rustic plating. The overall tone is inviting and warm, with golden-hour hues. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. Lived-in, authentic home-cooked atmosphere. No plastic sheen, no artificial symmetry, no hands, no text, no watermarks. Indistinguishable from a professional cookbook photograph."
]
